---
import BaseLayout from '../../components/layout/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Research-led thought leadership"
  description="Generate original evidence through focused qualitative research, then turn it into a distinctive argument, report and thought-leadership programme."
  pageType="service"
>
  <article class="container-site py-20">
    <div class="service-inner">
      <header class="mb-16">
        <p class="t-label mb-6">Research-led thought leadership</p>
        <h1 class="t-display mb-6">Build the evidence behind a point of view worth hearing.</h1>
        <div class="prose mb-8">
          <p>You have an important question about your market, customers or category—but not yet enough original evidence to answer it with authority.</p>
          <p>I help you define what is worth learning, generate focused qualitative evidence and turn that understanding into a distinctive argument, flagship report and wider thought-leadership programme.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="facts mb-8">
          <div><span>Starting point</span><strong>An important unanswered question</strong></div>
          <div><span>Approach</span><strong>Focused qualitative enquiry</strong></div>
          <div><span>Outcome</span><strong>Evidence, argument and activation</strong></div>
        </div>
        <div class="ctas">
          <a class="button" href="mailto:asavin@editorialintelligence.co?subject=Research-led%20thought%20leadership%20enquiry">Discuss the question</a>
          <a class="text-link" href="#engagement">See how the engagement works ↓</a>
        </div>
      </header>

      <hr class="divider mb-16" />
      <section class="mb-16">
        <p class="t-label mb-4">Who it is for</p>
        <h2 class="service-h2 mb-6">When borrowed evidence is no longer enough</h2>
        <div class="prose mb-8">
          <p>This work is for B2B organisations that want to lead a useful market conversation, but cannot yet support their position with sufficient original evidence.</p>
        </div>
        <ul class="signal-list">
          <li>You have a strong hypothesis but need to test it with practitioners or customers.</li>
          <li>Your category relies on familiar claims that competitors can make just as easily.</li>
          <li>Your executives have valuable questions and experience, but no shared evidence base.</li>
          <li>You want a report that begins with genuine learning rather than a predetermined campaign message.</li>
          <li>You need one coherent argument that can support content, conversations and decisions over time.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <hr class="divider mb-16" />
      <section id="engagement" class="mb-16">
        <p class="t-label mb-4">The engagement</p>
        <h2 class="service-h2 mb-8">From knowledge gap to usable point of view</h2>
        <div class="steps">
          <div><span>01</span><p><strong>Define the question</strong>Clarify what the organisation needs to understand, what it already knows and which assumptions need testing.</p></div>
          <div><span>02</span><p><strong>Design the enquiry</strong>Set the participant profile, discussion guide, evidence framework and practical research scope.</p></div>
          <div><span>03</span><p><strong>Generate evidence</strong>Gather original qualitative evidence through practitioner, customer, executive or stakeholder interviews and structured conversations.</p></div>
          <div><span>04</span><p><strong>Synthesise the findings</strong>Identify patterns, tensions, exceptions and knowledge gaps rather than selecting quotations to fit a pre-agreed claim.</p></div>
          <div><span>05</span><p><strong>Develop the argument</strong>Turn the evidence into a clear, defensible interpretation with supporting claims and appropriate qualifications.</p></div>
          <div><span>06</span><p><strong>Activate and learn</strong>Build the flagship output and a plan for extending, testing and improving the thinking through future content and conversations.</p></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <hr class="divider mb-16" />
      <section class="mb-16">
        <p class="t-label mb-4">What you leave with</p>
        <h2 class="service-h2 mb-8">Understanding first. Content second.</h2>
        <div class="output-grid">
          <div><strong>Evidence base</strong><p>Structured findings, themes, tensions and useful participant evidence.</p></div>
          <div><strong>Distinctive argument</strong><p>A central point of view grounded in what the enquiry genuinely revealed.</p></div>
          <div><strong>Flagship report</strong><p>A credible editorial expression of the evidence and its implications.</p></div>
          <div><strong>Content programme</strong><p>A practical architecture for articles, executive content, events, video and distribution.</p></div>
          <div><strong>Evidence gaps</strong><p>A clear account of what remains uncertain and worth investigating next.</p></div>
          <div><strong>Learning plan</strong><p>A way to capture response, add new evidence and strengthen the position over time.</p></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <hr class="divider mb-16" />
      <section class="mb-16">
        <p class="t-label mb-4">The distinction</p>
        <h2 class="service-h2 mb-6">This is an Editorial Intelligence engagement—not standalone market research.</h2>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>Research is one capability within the wider methodology. The objective is not to deliver a dataset and leave. It is to understand what the evidence means, develop the organisation's point of view and create a system through which that understanding can influence its market and its own decisions.</p>
          <p>The scope is qualitative and editorial. Where a project requires large-scale polling, statistical validation or specialist market-research operations, I would work with an appropriate research partner rather than overstate the offer.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="closing-panel">
        <p class="t-label mb-6">Start with the question</p>
        <h2 class="service-h2 mb-4">What does your organisation need to understand before it has earned the right to make the argument?</h2>
        <div class="prose mb-8"><p>Tell me the question, what evidence you already have and what still feels uncertain. I will help you decide whether a research-led thought-leadership engagement is the right next step.</p></div>
        <a class="button" href="mailto:asavin@editorialintelligence.co?subject=Research-led%20thought%20leadership%20enquiry">Start a conversation</a>
        <p class="note">Interested in contributing to research about Editorial Intelligence itself? <a class="text-link" href="/compare-notes">Join a Compare Notes conversation →</a></p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .service-inner{max-width:44rem}.prose{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:1.25rem}.prose p{font-size:1rem;line-height:1.8;color:var(--color-ink-secondary)}.service-h2{font-family:var(--font-serif);font-size:clamp(1.15rem,2.5vw,1.45rem);font-weight:400;color:var(--color-ink)}.facts{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:1px;padding:1px;background:var(--color-rule);border-radius:4px;overflow:hidden}.facts div{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.35rem;padding:1rem;background:var(--color-surface-secondary)}.facts span{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:.65rem;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--color-accent)}.facts strong{font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;font-weight:400;color:var(--color-ink-secondary)}.ctas{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:1.5rem;flex-wrap:wrap}.button{display:inline-flex;padding:.75rem 1.25rem;border-radius:3px;background:var(--color-accent);color:var(--color-surface);font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:.72rem;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.05em;text-decoration:none}.button:hover{opacity:.85}.text-link{color:var(--color-accent);text-decoration:none;font-size:.875rem}.signal-list{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.75rem}.signal-list li{position:relative;padding-left:1.25rem;color:var(--color-ink-secondary);line-height:1.7}.signal-list li::before{content:'→';position:absolute;left:0;color:var(--color-accent)}.steps{display:flex;flex-direction:column;border:1px solid var(--color-rule);border-radius:4px;overflow:hidden}.steps>div{display:flex;gap:1.25rem;padding:1.25rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-rule);background:var(--color-surface-secondary)}.steps>div:last-child{border-bottom:0}.steps span{min-width:1.5rem;padding-top:.15rem;font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:.72rem;color:var(--color-accent)}.steps p{margin:0;font-size:.875rem;line-height:1.7;color:var(--color-ink-tertiary)}.steps strong,.output-grid strong{display:block;margin-bottom:.25rem;color:var(--color-ink);font-weight:500}.output-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1px;padding:1px;background:var(--color-rule);border-radius:4px;overflow:hidden}.output-grid div{padding:1.25rem;background:var(--color-surface-secondary)}.output-grid p{font-size:.8125rem;line-height:1.65;color:var(--color-ink-tertiary)}.closing-panel{padding:1.5rem;border:1px solid var(--color-rule);border-left:2px solid var(--color-accent);border-radius:4px;background:var(--color-surface-secondary)}.note{margin-top:1.25rem;font-size:.8125rem;line-height:1.7;color:var(--color-ink-tertiary)}@media(max-width:640px){.facts,.output-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
